WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to shift gears,
because based on everything --

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:06.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:07.440 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I feel -- there you go.
Thank you.

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:14.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's -- because I --
-My Sinéad O'Connor look.

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:16.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
This is for the play.

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:17.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But this does speak --
-Yes.

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:21.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It speaks to the amazing
breadth you have as an actor.

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:22.355 line:92%
Because this play you're doing,

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:26.259 size:84% position:42%
"Angels in America",
is a very serious play.

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:27.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're playing Roy Cohn...
-Yes.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.163
-...who is a real person.
-The Dr. Frankenstein to --

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:31.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Donald Trump's monster.

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:33.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, he was Donald Trump's
lawyer and mentor.

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:34.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Lawyer and mentor.
-And --

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:35.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, he paid him to do all
his dirty work,

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:36.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
which, I know, is shocking.
-Yeah.

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:39.773
-Donald Trump paying someone --
-To do his dirty work.

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:41.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-How -- you played this part

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:44.044
before in London.
-Yes, seven months I was there.

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:45.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Seven months. So -- and how
has it been so far?

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:49.382
How has it been returning to it?
-It's...let's put it this way,

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:54.120
I've been an actor for 43 years.
This is my 21st Broadway show.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:59.592
And I would say this is probably
the greatest ensemble of actors

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:04.664
I've ever worked with. I mean,
certainly the play, you know,

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:06.066 line:92%
is a Pulitzer Prize-winner.

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:08.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's incredibly funny
and profoundly moving piece.

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:11.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's all centered around
Andrew Garfield,

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:13.907
who plays the leading character,
Prior Walter.

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:16.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he's giving
a magnificent performance.

00:01:16.276 --> 00:01:21.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I think if people know
the play,

00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:24.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
you've never quite seen it
done like this.

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:26.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
Marianne Elliott
is the director.

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:28.321 size:88% position:44% line:92%
She did the "War Horse,"

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:29.556
"The Curious Incident of the Dog
in the Nighttime."

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:34.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's an incredibly gifted
and inspiring director.

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:36.930 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this is -- if you think
you've seen it,

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.331 line:92%
you haven't seen this version,

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:40.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's well worth
checking out.

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:41.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I can't wait.
-It's a magnificent play.

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:42.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It really is
a magnificent play.

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:44.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I really can't wait to see
you doing it.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:48.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to ask about something
else that's serious --

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:49.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But you actually have

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:50.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
a little history with this
as well.

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:51.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, obviously,
Harvey Weinstein came up

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:53.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
a little bit last night.
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:55.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's come up a fair amount,
as well he should.

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:58.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have -- you had had
a history with him for years

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:01.988
and you had not gotten along
with him for a very long time.

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:05.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I'll tell you what
happened to Harvey Weinstein.

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:07.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
Couldn't have happened
to a nicer guy.

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:08.061 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:09.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm putting my glasses
back on for this.

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:11.297 size:75% position:38%
-Yeah, yeah, please.
-Harvey Weinstein --

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:14.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
in 2000, my publicist called
and said,

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.336
"Harvey Weinstein would like you
to host a fundraiser

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:19.072 size:84% position:42%
for Hillary Clinton."
And he said, "you know,

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:20.607 line:92%
"he produces a lot of movies.

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:22.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
It wouldn't be bad to be
on his good side."

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:23.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-So I said, "okay."

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:26.479
And they said, "he wants
to pre-screen the jokes,"

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:29.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
because someone else hosted
a fundraiser

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:30.450 line:92%
and said something offensive

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:31.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he doesn't want
to go through that again.

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:34.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "okay."
But I was working with some

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
writers from Letterman,
actually, and who

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:39.592
I wasn't worried and we weren't
going to do anything offensive.

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:43.263
So we never heard from him
until the night of the show.

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:46.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then about an hour
beforehand, he came backstage

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:49.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
and like, Tony Soprano,
and was screaming.

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:51.104
You know, "you got to cut this,
you got to cut that.

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:52.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't understand this.
This sucks."

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:57.710
And I said, "no, it's too late.
I can't do that now."

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:00.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's -- you know.
And as we know --

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:02.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Now, he doesn't take no

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:03.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
for an answer easily.
-Yeah.

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:06.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]
-So -- so...

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:09.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter and applause ]
Things got heated.

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:11.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
[ Applause ]

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:13.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And unpleasantries
were exchanged.

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:15.328
And he said, you know, "I'll get
someone else to do it."

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:17.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "fine, I think I saw
Regis Philbin out there.

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:21.267
See if he's available."
And he started to push me

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:25.205
into a corner and he's screaming
at me and it crescendoed with,

00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:27.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'll ruin you," he said.
"I'll ruin you."

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:31.077
And I said, "you can't hurt me.
I don't have a film career."

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:33.313 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:34.614 line:92%
So the next thing I know,

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:36.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm called up to see
Hillary Clinton.

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:39.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
She got out of her coffin.
She said --

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:40.954 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:44.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
She says, "listen, you know,
I apologize for Harvey.

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:47.694
"But cut these jokes because
it'll only -- it'll just make

00:03:47.694 --> 00:03:51.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
life easier for all of us."
And I said, I gave in,

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:52.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I said, okay.
So we do the show.

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:55.868
In the middle of the show,
I'm supposed to introduce Cher.

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
So then they come to me
and they say,

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:59.706 line:92%
"Cher is stuck in traffic."

00:03:59.706 --> 00:04:02.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now when have you
last heard that?

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:03.243 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:05.245
When you're doing a show.
Cher is stuck in traffic.

00:04:05.245 --> 00:04:07.080
They said, "you're going do have
to fill." So I go --

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:09.382
-Which is a nightmare for anyone
hosting anything.

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:10.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-It's the last thing

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:11.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
you want to hear.
-You gotta fill.

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:13.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So I went out and I said,

00:04:13.553 --> 00:04:14.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'm sorry,
ladies and gentlemen,

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:16.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Cher, who was supposed
to be here,

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:19.692
had to stop to have some
emergency plastic surgery."

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:22.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
"So in the meantime,

00:04:22.462 --> 00:04:23.496 line:92%
"I'm going to do all the jokes

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:25.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Harvey Weinstein
made me cut."

00:04:25.565 --> 00:04:30.903 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:35.608 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:39.479
"If you find me in the Hudson
tomorrow, you'll know why."

00:04:39.479 --> 00:04:40.313 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:42.582
-It is so wonderful to see you
each and every time you're here.

00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:43.349 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Thank you, thank you.

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:45.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Give it to for Nathan Lane,
everybody.

